## Get Last Value

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/feeds/{feed_key}/data/last_value</code></div>

```shell
# plain text value of the most recent data point
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/feeds/{feed_key}/data/last_value

# the most recent data point as JSON
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" "https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/feeds/{feed_key}/data/last_value?type=json"

# value,lat,lon,ele as CSV
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" "https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/feeds/{feed_key}/data/last_value?type=csv"
```

> Response Sample (no `type`, `text/plain`):

```text
22.5
```

> Response Sample (`type=json`):

```json
{
  "id": "0F2ZQ4XJ6M3K8N1E7B9D5C0V4T",
  "value": "22.5",
  "feed_id": 1234,
  "feed_key": "temperature",
  "created_at": "2026-01-01T12:00:00Z",
  "created_epoch": 1767268800,
  "expiration": "2026-01-31T12:00:00Z"
}
```

> Response Sample (`type=csv`, `text/plain`):

```text
22.5,40.7,-74.0,10.0
```

Returns the most recent value in the feed without paging through the data list. This is the same value you receive when subscribing to the feed's `/get` MQTT topic. Unlike `first`, `next` and `previous`, it works with read-only access, so it can also be used on public feeds.

With no `type` (or any unrecognized `type`) the response is the bare value as plain text. If the feed has never received data the response is a `404`.

### Path Parameters

Parameter | Type    | Required  | Description
--------- | ------- | --------- | -----------------------
username  | string  | true      | a valid username string
feed_key  | string  | true      | a valid feed key

### Query Parameters

Parameter | Type    | Required  | Description
--------- | ------- | --------- | -----------------------
type      | string  | false     | `json` returns the data record as JSON; `csv` returns `value,lat,lon,ele` (lat, lon and ele are blank when not set). Anything else returns the value only.


