## Download Feed Data

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-post">POST</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/feeds/{feed_key}/data/download.csv</code></div>
> <div class="http"><span class="method-post">POST</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/feeds/{feed_key}/data/download.json</code></div>
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/feeds/{feed_key}/data/download/status</code></div>

```shell
# request a CSV export of all data in the feed (use download.json for JSON)
$ curl -X POST -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/feeds/{feed_key}/data/download.csv

# check progress and get a download link
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/feeds/{feed_key}/data/download/status
```

> Response Sample (POST):

```json
{
  "status": "ok"
}
```

> Response Sample (GET status):

```json
{
  "feed_id": 1234,
  "generated_at": "2026-01-01T12:05:00Z",
  "limited": true,
  "timeout": "540",
  "downloads": [
    {
      "url": "https://example.com/downloads/data.csv?expires=1767269160",
      "description": "Temperature CSV requested by {username}",
      "token": "a1b2c3d4e5f6",
      "state": "completed",
      "progress_percentage": 100.0,
      "file_size": "1.2 MB",
      "started_at": "2026-01-01T12:00:05Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-01-01T12:00:41Z"
    }
  ]
}
```

Requests an export of the complete data history of a feed you own. The export is built in the background, so the `POST` only queues it and returns `{"status": "ok"}`. The file format is chosen by the URL extension, `.csv` or `.json`; a request without one is not accepted.

To get the file, poll the status endpoint. It lists the feed's five most recent downloads. Each entry has a `state` (`building`, `completed`, or `error`), a `progress_percentage`, and a `url` for the file. The `url` expires after about a minute, so request the status again whenever you need a fresh link.

Only one download can be requested per feed every 10 minutes. A second request inside that window returns a `429` with an error message, plus these headers:

Header | Description
------ | -----------
X-RateLimit-LimitSeconds | the length of the cooldown window, in seconds
X-RateLimit-Timeout | seconds remaining until another download can be requested

The status response reports the same cooldown: `limited` is `true` and `timeout` holds the seconds remaining while the cooldown is active. This is separate from the data rate limit, see Rate Limiting.

### Path Parameters

Parameter | Type    | Required  | Description
--------- | ------- | --------- | -----------------------
username  | string  | true      | your username; downloads are only available for your own feeds
feed_key  | string  | true      | a valid feed key


## Download All Account Data

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-post">POST</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/download</code></div>
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/download/status</code></div>

```shell
# request an export of all your data
$ curl -X POST -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/download

# check progress and get a download link
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/download/status
```

> Response Sample (POST):

```json
{
  "status": "ok"
}
```

Queues an export of all of your account's data. It works like the feed download above: the `POST` returns `{"status": "ok"}`, and the status endpoint (same response format, without `feed_id`) lists your five most recent account downloads with their `state`, `progress_percentage` and expiring `url`. Only one account download can be requested every 24 hours; a request during the cooldown returns a `429` with the `X-RateLimit-LimitSeconds` and `X-RateLimit-Timeout` headers.

### Path Parameters

Parameter | Type    | Required  | Description
--------- | ------- | --------- | -----------------------
username  | string  | true      | your username


